  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mapping opportunities for sustainable agriculture in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Egypt&#x2019;s agricultural sector faces increasing water scarcity and the threats of climate change. At the same time, there is an increasing demand for safe and hygienic produce. A range of climate-smart technologies is necessary to address climate change and capitalize on lucrative agricultural markets. In September 2021, eleven Dutch companies visited Egypt to explore opportunities for cooperation, trade and investment in climate-smart agriculture. This project aims to capitalize on the connections built and the ideas initiated during this tour. It will connect local demand and potential Dutch supply to find the currently best matches. It will lead to one-to-one business cases and a consortium of Egyptian-Dutch companies that will work on implementing and adapting climate-smart technologies in Egypt.</narrative>
  </description>
